{
 "description": "C.2 from an imitation start (the plan review's option D; description, discarded seeds).\n\nSix sep-CMA designs reached the same basin: constant outputs set by the readout's biases, scoring\nabout 9.3-9.5 on v4's D_fit, with no responsive network nearby scoring better. Here C.2 starts from\na responsive network trained to act like a teacher, then sep-CMA refines it.\n\n- The teacher: C.1's 26-parameter warm probe answer on v4 (Logbook 125, `mechanism_ondwell.json`;\n  passes v4 in 4 of 5 discarded populations).\n- The student: the encoded connectome under per-ligand tying with four pool centres (136), the\n  soft cap 2\u00b7tanh(x/2), the graded box (wiring scales on [0, 0.75], sensory gains on [-2, 2]) and\n  the saturation guard, as `staged_bc.py` applies them (no package code changes).\n- The rollouts: on D_fit's two assays (Scheer's small lawn and uniform well), 100 animals each\n  (712,000,000 + i, and 712,100,000 + i), the teacher drives; on the same senses a shadow C.2\n  advances its own modulator concentrations, and each second's C.2 state (food features, its\n  modulators, the intake drive) is stored beside the teacher's raw action.\n- The training: Adam (lr 0.01, batches of 4,096) on C.2's learnable encoder tensors and centres,\n  minimising the squared error between C.2's squashed mean action and the teacher's raw action;\n  every 20 steps the vector is projected onto the graded box. Three rounds of 20 epochs, the shadow\n  re-rolled before each with the trained network, so its modulators follow its own activity.\n- The refinement: sep-CMA from the imitation answer, sigma0 0.1, v4's ranking score on D_fit with\n  the guard, CMA 9476, fit animals 714,000,000, 200 generations on 16 workers; checkpoints every 50\n  generations graded on 715,000,000, profiled as `staged_bc.py` profiles.\n\nRun from the repository root.\n",
